CommitDate: Thu Sep 24 13:01:37 2026 -0500

    fix: AUG-061 percent-encode every URL the CLI builds (spaced names no longer kill the verb).
    
    `python3 auger.py --namespace 'ns with space' --project-id 'Test Project' feedback` died with a
    raw `http.client.InvalidURL` traceback. The crash was client-side: `http.client` validates the
    request line and refuses a raw space BEFORE anything is sent — so a name with a space did not
    produce a wrong answer, it killed the verb, in every verb, wherever the text landed.
    
    Root cause: URLs were built by f-string interpolation at eight sites, with no encoding anywhere.
    They now all go through one boundary:
    
    - `url_seg()` — path segments and query KEYS, `safe=""`. `quote`'s default `safe="/"` is wrong
      here: a namespace named `a/b` would silently become two path segments (a different table).
    - `encode_query()` — the structure (`&`, the first `=` of each pair, and the `op.` after it) stays
      literal and only the value text is encoded. `,` stays readable ON PURPOSE: postgrest uses it as a
      list separator (`select=id,name`, `order=domain.asc,id.asc`, `in=(a,b)`).
    - `ns_tables_path()` — the four hand-interpolated `/api/ns/{ns}/tables` sites (declared_columns,
      init's two existence verifications, and the declaration read-back).
    
    Two further same-class sites the grep for raw URL f-strings found, not named in the row:
    `delete_namespace` (`/api/namespaces/{ns}` — `teardown` on a spaced namespace crashed the same way)
    and `recall` (`namespace={ns}`; `q` was already quoted, the namespace was not).
    
    Verified live against DuckBrain (127.0.0.1:3000):
    
    - the reported command line now exits 1 with a named substrate answer — `Table 'project' not found
      in namespace 'ns with space'` — and no traceback;
    - a project STORED under the id `Test Project` is found by `status`, `feedback` and `dump` with
      `--project-id 'Test Project'`. The encoded `eq.Test%20Project` value comes back decoded by the
      service, which is what makes this a fix rather than a string that merely parses;
    - `GET /api/ns/auger%20061%20does%20not%20exist/tables` answers 200 with
      `"namespace": "auger 061 does not exist"` — the path half decodes too.
    
    Tests: tests/test_auger.py grows a "url encoding (AUG-061)" section — spaced path segment, spaced
    filter value, both at once, the live `status` round trip on a spaced project id, the reported
    command line as a non-crash, the live path-decoding probe, `recall`/`delete_namespace` URL capture,
    plus two controls that keep the rest honest: the pre-fix URL is proved STILL rejected by the same
    `http.client` validator (so the encoding assertions cannot go vacuous), and the query shapes the
    rest of the suite depends on are pinned unchanged. RED first: 9 of the 11 encoding cases fail on
    the pre-fix tree; the two controls pass by design.
    
    `_req` (retry/backoff) is untouched.
    
    `bash tests/gate.sh`: GATE PASS.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
